   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "customData": {
    "gen": "kerd"
   },
   "roundness": null,
   "text": "Two things the ratified design gets wrong",
   "fontSize": 14,
   "fontFamily": 6,
   "textAlign": "center",
   "verticalAlign": "middle",
   "containerId": "r1037",
   "originalText": "Two things the ratified design gets wrong",
   "autoResize": true,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "t1039",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 678,
   "y": 1568,
   "width": 429.00000000000006,
   "height": 195.0,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 2,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 1,
   "opacity": 100,
   "groupIds": [],
   "frameId": null,
   "index": "a0039",
   "seed": 17273,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 33507,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": [],
   "updated": 1785400000000,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "customData": {
    "gen": "kerd"
   },
   "roundness": null,
   "text": "FINAL IS UNFALSIFIABLE.  Doorstop's `reviewed` is a SHA256\nfingerprint of the item, not a label. MEASURED: editing one line\nof a requirement's text immediately reported 'unreviewed\nchanges'. Kerd's `final` survives any later edit - so an approval\ncannot be told from one whose subject changed underneath it.\n  -> the record stores a hash of the statement at approval.\n     edit the statement and the state degrades, by construction.\n\nA STATE OWES NOTHING.  Sphinx-Needs attaches OBLIGATIONS to a\nstate. MEASURED: 'a fun in status final must be verified_by at\nleast one tst' produced a real refusal.\n  -> the producer's own G0-G8 gates already state the\n     obligations. In PROSE. this is their machine form.",
   "fontSize": 12,
   "fontFamily": 6,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "originalText": "FINAL IS UNFALSIFIABLE.  Doorstop's `reviewed` is a SHA256\nfingerprint of the item, not a label. MEASURED: editing one line\nof a requirement's text immediately reported 'unreviewed\nchanges'. Kerd's `final` survives any later edit - so an approval\ncannot be told from one whose subject changed underneath it.\n  -> the record stores a hash of the statement at approval.\n     edit the statement and the state degrades, by construction.\n\nA STATE OWES NOTHING.  Sphinx-Needs attaches OBLIGATIONS to a\nstate. MEASURED: 'a fun in status final must be verified_by at\nleast one tst' produced a real refusal.\n  -> the producer's own G0-G8 gates already state the\n     obligations. In PROSE. this is their machine form.",
   "autoResize": true,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "t1040",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 1320,
   "y": 1504,
   "width": 165.0,
   "height": 225.0,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#e03131",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
