   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "customData": {
    "gen": "kerd"
   },
   "roundness": null,
   "text": "Named before the design, not discovered during it",
   "fontSize": 14,
   "fontFamily": 6,
   "textAlign": "center",
   "verticalAlign": "middle",
   "containerId": "r1051",
   "originalText": "Named before the design, not discovered during it",
   "autoResize": true,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "t1053",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 678,
   "y": 2276,
   "width": 409.20000000000005,
   "height": 195.0,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 2,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 1,
   "opacity": 100,
   "groupIds": [],
   "frameId": null,
   "index": "a0053",
   "seed": 17371,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 33689,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": [],
   "updated": 1785400000000,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "customData": {
    "gen": "kerd"
   },
   "roundness": null,
   "text": "1. the register stops being one file. catalog, disposition,\n   register and relations are four declared things - which is\n   NFR-004 pressure ('not scatter artifacts') and must be\n   argued, not assumed. one directory, four files, is the\n   defensible reading.\n\n2. a block format is harder to scan raw than a table. the VIEW\n   answers it - but only once the board exists, and the board\n   is unbuilt.\n\n3. fingerprinted approval means a state can change without a\n   human acting. that is the point, and it will surprise\n   someone the first time it fires.",
   "fontSize": 12,
   "fontFamily": 6,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "originalText": "1. the register stops being one file. catalog, disposition,\n   register and relations are four declared things - which is\n   NFR-004 pressure ('not scatter artifacts') and must be\n   argued, not assumed. one directory, four files, is the\n   defensible reading.\n\n2. a block format is harder to scan raw than a table. the VIEW\n   answers it - but only once the board exists, and the board\n   is unbuilt.\n\n3. fingerprinted approval means a state can change without a\n   human acting. that is the point, and it will surprise\n   someone the first time it fires.",
   "autoResize": true,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "t1054",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 1320,
   "y": 2212,
   "width": 165.0,
   "height": 90.0,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#e03131",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 2,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 1,
   "opacity": 100,
   "groupIds": [],
   "frameId": null,
   "index": "a0054",
   "seed": 17378,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 33702,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": [],
   "updated": 1785400000000,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "customData": {
    "gen": "kerd"
   },
   "roundness": null,
   "text": "none of these is a\nblocker. all three are\nunqualified, which is the\ndangerous state - a named\nunsized risk reads as\nmanaged.",
   "fontSize": 12,
   "fontFamily": 6,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "originalText": "none of these is a\nblocker. all three are\nunqualified, which is the\ndangerous state - a named\nunsized risk reads as\nmanaged.",
   "autoResize": true,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  }
